WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:06.215
♪♪

00:00:06.215 --> 00:00:10.219
David Attenborough:
Dawn, on the shore of the
ancient Tethys Sea.

00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:11.929
♪♪

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:15.766
David Attenborough:
And hundreds of tiny turtle
hatchlings are on the move.

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:18.852
♪♪

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:22.689
David Attenborough:
Instinctively, they race towards
the safety of the water.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:28.070
♪♪

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.697
David Attenborough:
They've been spotted by a
hunter.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:35.827
♪♪

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:37.871
(Exhale)

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:38.789
(Sniffing)

00:00:38.789 --> 00:00:43.043
♪♪

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.544
(Sniffing)

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:50.050
David Attenborough:
A young T-Rex, still sporting a
juvenile's feathery coat

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:57.516
♪♪

00:00:57.516 --> 00:00:59.726
David Attenborough:
He's got the killer instinct.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.520
♪♪

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:06.275
David Attenborough:
But his problem is...
inexperience.”

00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:07.859
(Mild growl)

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:09.778
(Water noise)

00:01:09.778 --> 00:01:11.697
David Attenborough:
This could take some time.

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:12.489
(Waves crashing)

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:23.083
♪♪

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:27.921
David Attenborough:
A full grown T-Rex is the
planet's most powerful predator,

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:31.049
(Heavy exhale)
♪♪

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:34.219
David Attenborough:
but today, he's just being
Father.

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:37.723
♪♪

